{
  "description": "Preserve Self-EvolveRec’s diagnostic interface while adapting its probes to the actual GRU4Rec model. DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader) returns measured metrics and explicit metric_definitions. diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis) converts these results into an evidence-based interpretation prompt.",
  "motivation": "Architecture-aware diagnostics can identify weaknesses in sequential recommendation without relying on unavailable reviews, ratings, product attributes, or simulated user traits. Model selection remains grounded in macro-average validation HR@10 across all four datasets.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain the host ModelView interfaces: model, item_emb, log2feats(sequence), predict_score(features, items), user_train, meta_data, and review_data. Consume batches shaped B x L as (None, sequence, positive, negative), exclude padding from measurements, and use the final nonpadding position for left-padded sequence readout. Report unavailable signals as unavailable. Preserve five real training users per category for full-catalog unseen-item recommendations. Keep one independently trained GRU4Rec model per category, dataset routing, and checkpoint/predictor consistency. Diagnostics must not access hidden test data or replace the pinned validation evaluator.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe:\n    init(view, device): retain actual model and compatibility interfaces\n    run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n        preserve model training state; enter evaluation mode\n        under no_grad:\n            for _, sequence, positive, negative in train_loader:\n                compute features through view.log2feats(sequence)\n                score items through view.predict_score(features, items)\n                accumulate applicable measurements over valid positions\n        restore model training state\n        return {metrics: measured_results, metric_definitions: definitions}\n\ndef diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n    include measured metrics, definitions, and missing-signal limitations\n    request evidence-supported GRU4Rec improvement hypotheses\n    preserve single-model and fixed-evaluation constraints",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Makes diagnostic interpretation explicitly aware of model-family interfaces and observable data.",
    "negative": "Primarily an integration contract rather than a new recommendation algorithm; score uses a 1–10 scale."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Could support targeted architecture and training improvements through repeatable, interpretable measurements.",
    "negative": "Diagnostic usefulness and resulting HR@10 gains require experimental validation."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The fixed adapter interfaces and batch format provide a clear implementation boundary.",
    "negative": "Correct padding, feature alignment, metric aggregation, and architecture compatibility require care; higher scores indicate greater difficulty."
  }
}
